A||||1||Larry Miller||Changing CV Boots
Z||000000||Larry Miller||05-05-99||04:46 PM||||How tough is it to change rear driver side CV boot? Any special tools or tips?
Z||000001||theogre||05-06-99||07:29 AM||||If you are <b>sure</b> the axle is good, there are a couple options.<p>a "split boot" kit can be installed with no disassembly. you may need a tool for the clamps, it depends on what kit you get. You can usually do this right on the car.<p>to install an OEM style one piece boot, you need to remove the axle from the car. you then must disassemble the CV joint. This does require some tools to be done without damaging anything. you will also need the crimp tool for the boot clamps.<p>It is probably easier, and for most people safer, to install a reconditioned, or good used, axle if you don't like the idea of the split boot kit. A reconditioned axle generally runs around 100$, and there will likely be a core charge on it.
